CM ============================================================================
CM  INTEGRATED ANTENNA ANALYZER - TEST REFERENCE MODELS
CM  ANTENNA: QUARTER-WAVE OPEN STUB (Resonance Algorithm Test)
CM  PURPOSE: Verify resonance detection algorithm (Im(Z) = 0 finder)
CM  TYPE: Open-circuit transmission line stub, vertical orientation
CM ============================================================================
CM
CM  STUB SPECIFICATIONS:
CM    Frequency: 100.0 MHz (arbitrary test frequency)
CM    Wavelength λ = 3.0 m
CM    Stub length: 0.25λ = 0.75 m
CM    Stub characteristic impedance: 50Ω (typical coax)
CM    Termination: OPEN (Z_load = ∞)
CM    Feed point impedance: 50Ω × j∞ (open circuit, purely capacitive)
CM
CM  ELECTRICAL BEHAVIOR:
CM    At 100.0 MHz (λ/4 length):
CM      Z_in = Z0 × cot(βl) = 50 × cot(π/2) = 50 × 0 = 0 + j∞ (open)
CM    At 200.0 MHz (λ/2 length): Z_in ≈ 0 + j0 (resonance point)
CM    At 50.0 MHz (λ/8 length): Z_in highly capacitive
CM
CM  RESONANCE ALGORITHM TEST:
CM    1. Sweep frequency: 50.0 to 250.0 MHz (5 MHz steps, 41 points)
CM    2. Algorithm should find: Im(Z) crosses zero at ~200 MHz
CM    3. At resonance: Z_real ≈ 0, Z_imag ≈ 0, Q undefined (low loss)
CM    4. Measure phase transition: Phase should flip 180° through resonance
CM    5. Verify: Phase unwrapping algorithm, reactance sign change detection
CM
CM  NEC2 MODEL (Approximation):
CM    - Segment of wire 0.75 m long, 1 mm diameter (thin wire approx of stub)
CM    - Open at far end (no connection to ground return)
CM    - Frequency sweep: 50 to 250 MHz (41 points)
CM    - This is a simplified model; actual coax stub would need TL model
CM
CM  NOTES:
CM    - NEC2 wire model is not ideal for transmission line, but gives
CM      qualitative resonance behavior
CM    - For precise stub behavior, use equivalent circuit model
CM    - This test verifies algorithm robustness with known resonance
CM
CE
GW 1 11 0 0 0 0 0 0.75 0.001
GE 0
GN 2 0 0 0 13.0 0.005
EX 0 1 6 0 1.0 0.0
FR 0 41 0 0 50.0 5.0
RP 0 361 1 1000 0.0 0.0 1.0 0.0
EN
